# Loose ends

Small things that came up while other work was going on. Written down in the turn they come up,
drained after an order resolves, at each checkpoint, and on request ("drain the loose ends").
The list is the inbox: only items not yet proposed. Once the drain proposes an item it moves to the pile
(`drain/pending/`) and leaves this list; an ask for the operator is raised from the pile.

Only the orchestrator writes it (`scripts/loose_ends.py`). An item is one or two sentences, at most
300 characters. This is never a work queue or a notebook: a finding that needs evidence, a cause, a
fix or its own worker is a work-order; a session plan belongs in `RESUME.md`. Nothing leaves the list
without the orchestrator's or the operator's decision: it is removed with `drop --to WO-NNN | P<n> |
brain:<page> | closed:<reason>` and git keeps the history. State is `new` or `declined: <reason>`.

